{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs records the one-resident rule as enforced behaviour, at head c50f0b0bb11014efa83420aede26f048cc2db675 on request/multi-resident-coordination, on main 2abe1cac. This replaces the retired candidate 31334f02a3d91910986a69630e403f2d709cfd5d at head 1ccad3e2. No documentation changed: all three pages are byte-identical to the reviewed candidate, and the whole delta from 1ccad3e2 is the one-byte final newline in internal/gitstore/gitstore.go.\n\nThree pages changed relative to main: docs/how-to/deploy-a-resident.md, docs/reference/gs/serve.md, docs/reference/architecture.md.\n\ndeploy-a-resident.md and serve.md both said \"Run exactly one. Nothing enforces it: there is no lock.\" Both now say what is enforced: the claim ref, the compare-and-swap that takes it, the bind-then-claim-then-serve order with ownership rather than binding authorizing service, the fail-closed probe, and the recovery command for a claim whose address can no longer be reached. serve.md's refusals table gains the three new refusals with their exact messages. deploy-a-resident.md states the operational cost honestly — an address reused by an unrelated program, or firewalled so probes time out, will keep refusing — and warns that clearing a claim while a service holds it is how the two rooms happen. architecture.md records the ownership-versus-advertisement contract in the nexus layer and names which package owns which half: internal/app owns the claim, internal/residentclient owns the probe and the duty to refuse any address that is not loopback, and the advertisement confers nothing. All three end on the same point, because a reader could otherwise take this for more than it is: the claim is coordination between cooperating residents, not a defence against a hostile local process, which already reaches the repository directly.\n\n#6349 had edited two of these pages, and both sides survived the earlier rebase: its citation repair in deploy-a-resident.md (frontmatter basis 68701f48) and its layer-6 and layer-7 paragraphs in architecture.md sit beside my sections, which codex's review at 1ccad3e2 confirmed.\n\nGates at this exact head: gofmt -l empty; go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... exit 0, 25 packages ok, including the four internal/docset documentation gates and the citation gate.\n\nThe live predecessor at this path is 48548e56b65589359dd6d25176de9b69a9453e7b at 2abe1cac, which is mine, so I can retire it myself at merge. There is no live artifact at the narrower docs/reference/architecture.md, so no bare supersession is needed there: docs is the single live granularity for this area.\n\nGoverned by request 78963842b2a9e67962d350db9a4d7bf72a07fe85 and direction proposal v3 998918b6a065170ab1558f6a1d1d37dc12477aa6, approved in report eb555d7eed99c8275b91cdf2224d6c0e1942cc01, ratified 726335d9.","body":{"commit":"c50f0b0bb11014efa83420aede26f048cc2db675","path":"docs"}}